 :question/id #uuid "33dc2ea2-d00c-5e39-945c-160ac13a087f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163030" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/ca0ff396606039accf8c3acb4fd1b8e505dd16d2fe9b765fcd5c043d1538a573.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=2{x}^{3}\\,\\text{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=2{x}^{3},\\,a=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{4}}{2}-0 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $8\\,\\text{kg}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163030/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163030"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163013/selection/4c46fc5ced918fea0e639e30f2eaa8365de048cdbbc1bab4307706e7e3cad94e" :answer/id #uuid "10d5a9a1-0f0f-5952-bdc3-14690dd35c74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163013/selection/55513f290f5cdf7d8326006301e28064916b4d6543cdff3eabb2487e9b62bf2e" :answer/id #uuid "a1df0822-126e-5b10-a1db-21188dc8bec1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163013/selection/a8cff032b6dcedd81dc19164df892a4991e1eabff9166206ba53973f973f3428" :answer/id #uuid "463abff5-66d0-55c3-9a67-478ade03c844" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163013/selection/1fd5bc06bcc6dbc518db4508cae87d487c69e854308c6dd578852e13c4e9380c" :answer/id #uuid "c292c459-aa87-5c26-aa31-2687886ea3ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163013/selection/1c1384cd7bf2f62005c7300ea1e18836f59043cb5b9b9db18c046cacaef69a3a" :answer/id #uuid "80fc6ef4-37f7-5889-8cd3-307d54f097fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163013/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1775140-24bb-5fe2-9572-f36ce5269808" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163013/selection/1fd5bc06bcc6dbc518db4508cae87d487c69e854308c6dd578852e13c4e9380c" :answer-field/choices ["q-163013/selection/4c46fc5ced918fea0e639e30f2eaa8365de048cdbbc1bab4307706e7e3cad94e" "q-163013/selection/55513f290f5cdf7d8326006301e28064916b4d6543cdff3eabb2487e9b62bf2e" "q-163013/selection/a8cff032b6dcedd81dc19164df892a4991e1eabff9166206ba53973f973f3428" "q-163013/selection/1fd5bc06bcc6dbc518db4508cae87d487c69e854308c6dd578852e13c4e9380c" "q-163013/selection/1c1384cd7bf2f62005c7300ea1e18836f59043cb5b9b9db18c046cacaef69a3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163013" :question/id #uuid "dc411752-e7d5-5473-a92e-af7ce4235eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-163013" :question/problem "The mass density function $\\lambda ,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ of a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2$ is given by $\\lambda (x)=3{x}^{2}+1,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by  \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=3{x}^{2}+1,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{2}+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}+x]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =({2}^{3}+2)-({1}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $8\\,\\text{kg}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163013/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163013"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163024/selection/a661134c972020a39ee9740e224b3e9b6f13dd5f97fcd95a6162a9167e751c17" :answer/id #uuid "b819fb76-f0bb-52a8-b292-01d9688c70d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163024/selection/f1006563a081de452d41fe7491beecd7832ae296b92612164446a2db0fb626d8" :answer/id #uuid "2074fe48-f43c-5b33-8df8-a17036cac77c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163024/selection/eb15f7eebb1e152801f9e9a0a5174a1e391ca3b1ff1fcebcfa1da9a3f068a227" :answer/id #uuid "801c2fb8-b57a-5d1c-9b4c-c0cbe3e22eb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163024/selection/3ae1ef22dfdc4b1cdcfa7704d9499cecebaccc99f015e3bd190a6283edf8cd59" :answer/id #uuid "b1bd2b04-4740-54f7-87dc-3308ef66e689" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163024/selection/924727ec80bb82b19f73ac54103ae9cf594ba370565fe906f587cd9bb636068f" :answer/id #uuid "f28bb641-56b2-53ea-82f3-37f5e46f2a7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163024/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "349f921d-73c7-5ab0-ab4f-20aa5eca12cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163024/selection/f1006563a081de452d41fe7491beecd7832ae296b92612164446a2db0fb626d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-163024/selection/a661134c972020a39ee9740e224b3e9b6f13dd5f97fcd95a6162a9167e751c17" "q-163024/selection/f1006563a081de452d41fe7491beecd7832ae296b92612164446a2db0fb626d8" "q-163024/selection/eb15f7eebb1e152801f9e9a0a5174a1e391ca3b1ff1fcebcfa1da9a3f068a227" "q-163024/selection/3ae1ef22dfdc4b1cdcfa7704d9499cecebaccc99f015e3bd190a6283edf8cd59" "q-163024/selection/924727ec80bb82b19f73ac54103ae9cf594ba370565fe906f587cd9bb636068f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163024" :question/id #uuid "4ccca339-64f3-5137-9985-a212fbf787d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-163024" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/d64311921135cf8dea0ec70bb0a83909fb1dba52664f4d6080de596be1693d5e.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}},\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}8{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-4{x}^{-2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{4}{1}) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $3\\,\\text{kg}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163024/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163024"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163023/selection/dfe6ed7e88310aeed7dfcea7d23901e02d9887857e089ca4c709b4bd4736bf77" :answer/id #uuid "f0cfba89-3ce3-5659-838e-728c888039de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163023/selection/eb089a35c11de99328701c870122e7d438407471b32acff4fde0412bf9b83cb1" :answer/id #uuid "48a3c1b7-21e2-5baf-bae6-140abb3a628c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163023/selection/217398de8bb232650b6e89c81bc6796de7d621cf453ce02d9c523087d9455b4c" :answer/id #uuid "00a1d592-1232-50d2-af2f-55d1e668817c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163023/selection/c67a3ec552f1fc69031b8a93ef8ac9e921eb079584bfc47f7a64ce2379d3abcb" :answer/id #uuid "528d87c7-a383-5408-83cb-5c005805f511" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163023/selection/cd60cc53a9cfba5ebafc7c887e2088b56beeea866d298f7e1385cb23d9990719" :answer/id #uuid "8523eb1e-51d4-571b-91a0-a2bc5230f09e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163023/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4237cfbe-c857-54ef-8c26-c86a6fe55c3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163023/selection/cd60cc53a9cfba5ebafc7c887e2088b56beeea866d298f7e1385cb23d9990719" :answer-field/choices ["q-163023/selection/dfe6ed7e88310aeed7dfcea7d23901e02d9887857e089ca4c709b4bd4736bf77" "q-163023/selection/eb089a35c11de99328701c870122e7d438407471b32acff4fde0412bf9b83cb1" "q-163023/selection/217398de8bb232650b6e89c81bc6796de7d621cf453ce02d9c523087d9455b4c" "q-163023/selection/c67a3ec552f1fc69031b8a93ef8ac9e921eb079584bfc47f7a64ce2379d3abcb" "q-163023/selection/cd60cc53a9cfba5ebafc7c887e2088b56beeea866d298f7e1385cb23d9990719"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163023" :question/id #uuid "c027f14f-4add-545b-a1e6-658b8f9d8813" :question/math-academy-id "q-163023" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/d0e2bd46bf7db6e20f321383e8e0440a2a86f263ce5eb256d20db71f5c632e27.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=6{x}^{2}-10\\,\\text{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=6{x}^{2}-10,\\,a=2,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}6{x}^{2}-10\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{x}^{3}-10x]_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 27-10\\cdot 3)-(2\\cdot 8-10\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $28\\,\\text{kg}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163023/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163023"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163027/selection/6cba2ef6a62ff40b8fff65566f1c3b484b83beeb81032a8cb54652945162980f" :answer/id #uuid "b465ec99-ee85-5e03-a67b-6a865f8facd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163027/selection/217398de8bb232650b6e89c81bc6796de7d621cf453ce02d9c523087d9455b4c" :answer/id #uuid "199e930f-42a2-514c-93be-b747ea5cc420" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163027/selection/42db993d011ad91495792f1f65dd834a8fbd211acea9160643edf39d18ffddf2" :answer/id #uuid "92da2784-bc65-5fa0-b114-edeb65061c2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163027/selection/55513f290f5cdf7d8326006301e28064916b4d6543cdff3eabb2487e9b62bf2e" :answer/id #uuid "2545c8fa-8dc0-5b48-9d05-139a622037d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163027/selection/4b6fe4a679339126e3109c83f74c346138ffa745bdba106b84669412ae819104" :answer/id #uuid "bcfde3e2-1c11-5354-a9f6-c5cace3b08ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163027/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b59cb92-eaa9-5e25-8c0c-18553a2d5817" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163027/selection/217398de8bb232650b6e89c81bc6796de7d621cf453ce02d9c523087d9455b4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-163027/selection/6cba2ef6a62ff40b8fff65566f1c3b484b83beeb81032a8cb54652945162980f" "q-163027/selection/217398de8bb232650b6e89c81bc6796de7d621cf453ce02d9c523087d9455b4c" "q-163027/selection/42db993d011ad91495792f1f65dd834a8fbd211acea9160643edf39d18ffddf2" "q-163027/selection/55513f290f5cdf7d8326006301e28064916b4d6543cdff3eabb2487e9b62bf2e" "q-163027/selection/4b6fe4a679339126e3109c83f74c346138ffa745bdba106b84669412ae819104"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163027" :question/id #uuid "4aa00abd-44ce-5eec-8222-ab2ef2eb803d" :question/math-academy-id "q-163027" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/32500120ed36acde90f5b27c44a6cf45f2d4766bacb5eb097debc0cd7117f27f.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=3{x}^{2}-x\\,\\text{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=3{x}^{2}-x,\\,a=1,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}3{x}^{2}-x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(27-\\frac{9}{2})-(1-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $22\\,\\text{kg}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163027/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163027"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163041/selection/408d6b6dae7728d49501277b6f33a16ea7b53b43eedb89258ce172de2a954e1d" :answer/id #uuid "a8d19e1b-691e-5b22-84f2-663e51aad86c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163041/selection/ec39c26889f195914090760cc04ef70bb7f61f40ce150ac1d11e7f59fab462b6" :answer/id #uuid "dbcffca4-4f0e-5ffe-b015-f90cb18f3473" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163041/selection/5d7504d1f4ce97a433b956b68ac2cbb2268eecf88e34512d7c880081bcad2899" :answer/id #uuid "c9b21594-5ff0-5192-8418-6c00c35d555d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163041/selection/c01e4667db65a4bbe28c2555e06cf62ae0f0a3b4ec8ecfe2bd72e56b842d3ab9" :answer/id #uuid "54a57188-be39-5dbd-ab67-7d55d1cd5cea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163041/selection/fe90678e55592d4eedc410d402f207331ca2cd8c380014171a78472a1e8a8c88" :answer/id #uuid "4c95a514-9354-571a-8661-02ccca1cccae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163041/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6647b0fe-5337-5e18-b21e-d07d66a446e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163041/selection/5d7504d1f4ce97a433b956b68ac2cbb2268eecf88e34512d7c880081bcad2899" :answer-field/choices ["q-163041/selection/408d6b6dae7728d49501277b6f33a16ea7b53b43eedb89258ce172de2a954e1d" "q-163041/selection/ec39c26889f195914090760cc04ef70bb7f61f40ce150ac1d11e7f59fab462b6" "q-163041/selection/5d7504d1f4ce97a433b956b68ac2cbb2268eecf88e34512d7c880081bcad2899" "q-163041/selection/c01e4667db65a4bbe28c2555e06cf62ae0f0a3b4ec8ecfe2bd72e56b842d3ab9" "q-163041/selection/fe90678e55592d4eedc410d402f207331ca2cd8c380014171a78472a1e8a8c88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163041" :question/id #uuid "51ab33b6-8bc7-58e3-84d1-57c89b0da879" :question/math-academy-id "q-163041" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/7f88ca365b75320795e9d38170a8586399d759696638a4bd78c73ca6c6f44b1a.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=4-x\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=4-x,\\,a=0,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot (4-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4x-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(2\\cdot {3}^{2}-\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3})-0 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163041/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163041"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163036/selection/5d7504d1f4ce97a433b956b68ac2cbb2268eecf88e34512d7c880081bcad2899" :answer/id #uuid "0037044b-3072-527e-8ac2-1b376f743163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163036/selection/2d3636214325310dd02231ec03a556f7efe5e73986e90e2cd03eeb749baae693" :answer/id #uuid "2c93a7a6-90fb-5930-b090-ce19a9936965" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163036/selection/c01e4667db65a4bbe28c2555e06cf62ae0f0a3b4ec8ecfe2bd72e56b842d3ab9" :answer/id #uuid "7df42914-ac94-5d0b-a1c3-856170711096" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163036/selection/4ffbceef34361ff5043704df8cfd06987a05f71ad715e903a4bbb70cf536be96" :answer/id #uuid "61eb5ea7-4724-5d42-b74f-ac12f085d3bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163036/selection/408d6b6dae7728d49501277b6f33a16ea7b53b43eedb89258ce172de2a954e1d" :answer/id #uuid "93871334-7775-52a4-aed7-3c5f84b07edb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163036/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "735e2c7f-3a8c-564a-b6a9-508b924dd3ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163036/selection/c01e4667db65a4bbe28c2555e06cf62ae0f0a3b4ec8ecfe2bd72e56b842d3ab9" :answer-field/choices ["q-163036/selection/5d7504d1f4ce97a433b956b68ac2cbb2268eecf88e34512d7c880081bcad2899" "q-163036/selection/2d3636214325310dd02231ec03a556f7efe5e73986e90e2cd03eeb749baae693" "q-163036/selection/c01e4667db65a4bbe28c2555e06cf62ae0f0a3b4ec8ecfe2bd72e56b842d3ab9" "q-163036/selection/4ffbceef34361ff5043704df8cfd06987a05f71ad715e903a4bbb70cf536be96" "q-163036/selection/408d6b6dae7728d49501277b6f33a16ea7b53b43eedb89258ce172de2a954e1d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163036" :question/id #uuid "1f5ebe42-9a69-55b4-85c3-da9b0cecac83" :question/math-academy-id "q-163036" :question/problem "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=6x,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=6x,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot 6x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({2}^{3}-{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163036/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163036"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186198565 :question/answer-fields 17592186194291] {:db/id "q-162948/selection/ma-v1/6075a9375152dd7cae4c0fccba26b5a142324c15d93ea6114255a193409e7ba3/2d3636214325310dd02231ec03a556f7efe5e73986e90e2cd03eeb749baae693" :answer/id #uuid 