3/2d3636214325310dd02231ec03a556f7efe5e73986e90e2cd03eeb749baae693" "q-162948/selection/ma-v1/6075a9375152dd7cae4c0fccba26b5a142324c15d93ea6114255a193409e7ba3/c01e4667db65a4bbe28c2555e06cf62ae0f0a3b4ec8ecfe2bd72e56b842d3ab9" "q-162948/selection/ma-v1/6075a9375152dd7cae4c0fccba26b5a142324c15d93ea6114255a193409e7ba3/d34a522b7a1b277a0208adb5b13ea8b1dadef7043b13035aad88064f31bb02bb" "q-162948/selection/ma-v1/6075a9375152dd7cae4c0fccba26b5a142324c15d93ea6114255a193409e7ba3/408d6b6dae7728d49501277b6f33a16ea7b53b43eedb89258ce172de2a954e1d" "q-162948/selection/ma-v1/6075a9375152dd7cae4c0fccba26b5a142324c15d93ea6114255a193409e7ba3/4e077343e079dd4aba5fb6e41a52f9fec8fb22c55cf9aa81cb767cf81e5a6874"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-162948"] :question/problem "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=4{x}^{2},$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=4{x}^{2},\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot 4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{4}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{4}-{1}^{4} \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162948/selection/ma-v1/6075a9375152dd7cae4c0fccba26b5a142324c15d93ea6114255a193409e7ba3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163042/selection/ec39c26889f195914090760cc04ef70bb7f61f40ce150ac1d11e7f59fab462b6" :answer/id #uuid "16a47f28-3f8a-5961-