89486a9d686" :question/math-academy-id "q-163042" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/887bc91e2565fa24630af4cb74b28723783e31f4769495f0a28a622d73d176de.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=6x+{x}^{2}\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=6x+{x}^{2},\\,a=0,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot (6x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{1}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =2.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $2.25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163042/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163042"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163039/selection/5d7504d1f4ce97a433b956b68ac2cbb2268eecf88e34512d7c880081bcad2899" :answer/id #uuid "38178331-bb47-587b-8899-fce443d7aefa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163039/selection/01e6aab67adb37cd4ad73d0f0842dc98467879884986a65a56b0cbce8fc4cca0" :answer/id #uuid "12bf9c26-f0e3-5951-a5e8-e9f8033e8147" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163039/selection/4ffbceef34361ff5043704df8cfd06987a05f71ad715e903a4bbb70cf536be96" :answer/id #uuid "e08ece88-bbe1-5197-859b-2bb1d4ed0ccd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163039/selection/4e077343e079dd4aba5fb6e41a52f9fec8fb22c55cf9aa81cb767cf81e5a6874" :answer/id #uuid "89436c32-92c9-5406-ad2d-4a625a0d3835" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163039/selection/dc022bb7917800a85ff6b11166c493c16e16e15ba23f0428630fd684235cce58" :answer/id #uuid "e464e2d9-6878-55c4-bf74-25881ea61159" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163039/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa5b343b-f410-5840-a849-0c64eb6a7b73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163039/selection/01e6aab67adb37cd4ad73d0f0842dc98467879884986a65a56b0cbce8fc4cca0" :answer-field/choices ["q-163039/selection/5d7504d1f4ce97a433b956b68ac2cbb2268eecf88e34512d7c880081bcad2899" "q-163039/selection/01e6aab67adb37cd4ad73d0f0842dc98467879884986a65a56b0cbce8fc4cca0" "q-163039/selection/4ffbceef34361ff5043704df8cfd06987a05f71ad715e903a4bbb70cf536be96" "q-163039/selection/4e077343e079dd4aba5fb6e41a52f9fec8fb22c55cf9aa81cb767cf81e5a6874" "q-163039/selection/dc022bb7917800a85ff6b11166c493c16e16e15ba23f0428630fd684235cce58"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163039" :question/id #uuid "d2c0bfdd-0747-5e9c-ade1-1661720da9c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-163039" :question/problem "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=3x+1,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=3x+1,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot (3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{2}+x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(8+\\frac{4}{2})-(1+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2} \\\\  & =8.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $8.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163039/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163039"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-162957"] :question/problem "Consider a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 2$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=3x.$ Given that the rod's mass is $6$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=3x,\\,a=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot 3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =8-0 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{8}{6}=\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163019/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "590747f0-3390-59a9-bcfb-336154057fa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163019/selection/5b6a7457ecf38e757655a8ab80cd7dca24376644ed8b5d929a23fb6af65f88f0" :answer/id #uuid "f562bc8d-9de9-551c-bb52-8f61c3c5b019" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163019/selection/0d247918008ed78cc89a6965d62d9f4a8fe02d275ec22142df80e82512aa1ea1" :answer/id #uuid "bcb55e2c-5a1d-5c94-aa07-6df8e1243983" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163019/selection/ea886782f883139045e5abc122fc35c608bfcc0ac4d51b469ff658e915045408" :answer/id #uuid "d9fadb95-93b4-5e40-bb4d-b894be05ecbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163019/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer/id #uuid "de7d8e04-be88-5c88-b506-a252c526fbde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163019/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1fe72d6a-b3a2-5534-8650-7399e9ca1230" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163019/selection/ea886782f883139045e5abc122fc35c608bfcc0ac4d51b469ff658e915045408" :answer-field/choices ["q-163019/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" "q-163019/selection/5b6a7457ecf38e757655a8ab80cd7dca24376644ed8b5d929a23fb6af65f88f0" "q-163019/selection/0d247918008ed78cc89a6965d62d9f4a8fe02d275ec22142df80e82512aa1ea1" "q-163019/selection/ea886782f883139045e5abc122fc35c608bfcc0ac4d51b469ff658e915045408" "q-163019/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163019" :question/id #uuid "fc0cd8c9-d9c9-59c8-af1b-b823ec38fb53" :question/math-academy-id "q-163019" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/887bc91e2565fa24630af4cb74b28723783e31f4769495f0a28a622d73d176de.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=x+{x}^{2}.$ Given that the mass of the rod is $\\frac{5}{6}$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=x+{x}^{2},\\,a=0,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nSo,  the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot (x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{7}{12})}{(\\frac{5}{6})}=\\frac{7}{10}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163019/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163019"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163016/selection/72443840a1994ef4e387277621cd8f464de0132f9c0b12ec6eac8b3cee6eca7d" :answer/id #uuid "295404d0-cf33-5d75-82fe-eceede4f9284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163016/selection/ace37c2040207cebb14b55c05840a4c383db24d63f2349cf49f8db6a85f5faeb" :answer/id #uuid "23596538-9f89-5745-9b75-6db8e3995fde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163016/selection/202bc41b151304c4674a49796c8c3aded4f6b45a4bf6c3104fde99e1c2b2e4db" :answer/id #uuid "04eba856-0799-5bf4-9634-5e476b6469d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{e-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163016/selection/f4b00c5c6581e3ab68e88e9a6af82078595a84f8397608447d5b9722315f15ac" :answer/id #uuid "73d2ccaf-a34c-5bb5-b9b8-f8fa4ca3594a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163016/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" :answer/id #uuid "ddc60c7f-fa54-5aaa-b1ab-59703a193cb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163016/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aff35934-5480-5c7f-9ed7-d1aec7bc49e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163016/selection/ace37c2040207cebb14b55c05840a4c383db24d63f2349cf49f8db6a85f5faeb" :answer-field/choices ["q-163016/selection/72443840a1994ef4e387277621cd8f464de0132f9c0b12ec6eac8b3cee6eca7d" "q-163016/selection/ace37c2040207cebb14b55c05840a4c383db24d63f2349cf49f8db6a85f5faeb" "q-163016/selection/202bc41b151304c4674a49796c8c3aded4f6b45a4bf6c3104fde99e1c2b2e4db" "q-163016/selection/f4b00c5c6581e3ab68e88e9a6af82078595a84f8397608447d5b9722315f15ac" "q-163016/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163016" :question/id #uuid "db4151bb-178b-55fb-96c6-b5798c6d3993" :question/math-academy-id "q-163016" :question/problem "Consider a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le e$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Given that the rod's mass is $1$ unit, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,a=1,\\,b=e.\n$$\n\nSo, the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =e-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{e-1}{1}=e-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163016/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163016"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162981/selection/bcbe057cec11b06e556ce6eb64efebcbc7b9b530f339b3d67669620f3e550dc2" :answer/id #uuid "e2efb028-c4d5-5671-9bc1-3c07e556802d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162981/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" :answer/id #uuid "aaba3ad6-c108-5ed6-9212-15d5c0cd34cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162981/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" :answer/id #uuid "85e5472e-4f59-57b0-8852-7a8d2e6e0843" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162981/selection/8e1065e0a433f859a01c77631b6451e105d707d70e2225dc268d4aa4c9c23074" :answer/id #uuid "ea3a311d-5a1e-5425-9566-352f6febc698" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162981/selection/5a23477d3a3ecf2c966b4121d1d4849908ae77a59c8159d472308b3a49408e87" :answer/id #uuid "4273ca3d-0355-50bc-9870-61cf6d377c14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{64}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162981/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc8b43c7-5669-51d0-926d-c16a7838488d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162981/selection/bcbe057cec11b06e556ce6eb64efebcbc7b9b530f339b3d67669620f3e550dc2" :answer-field/choices ["q-162981/selection/bcbe057cec11b06e556ce6eb64efebcbc7b9b530f339b3d67669620f3e550dc2" "q-162981/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" "q-162981/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" "q-162981/selection/8e1065e0a433f859a01c77631b6451e105d707d70e2225dc268d4aa4c9c23074" "q-162981/selection/5a23477d3a3ecf2c966b4121d1d4849908ae77a59c8159d472308b3a49408e87"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162981" :question/id #uuid "0d991181-2738-52fe-8913-289426ec5b40" :question/math-academy-id "q-162981" :question/problem "Consider a thin rod along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 4$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=\\sqrt{x}.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass of the rod." :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\sqrt{x},\\,a=0,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the mass of the rod is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {4}^{3/2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\cdot \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot {4}^{5/2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{64}{5})}{(\\frac{16}{3})}=\\frac{12}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-162981/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162981"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163022/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38" :answer/id #uuid "1524654e-ddbb-53b9-ac21-8632618dbb35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163022/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "c0e69c4b-f2fb-56e6-9009-be08e6e2172b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163022/selection/b937b5a9c9148a5914243385a1d84bacb019d6c5ff771ce01182a0f3091b9285" :answer/id #uuid "280e4b0c-fcb9-5957-ae7f-92daacca68f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163022/selection/fea7f6b22e69e29a9716f674d580a63eca4b26e1b4ae5c4f38b3026c28b2b97d" :answer/id #uuid "6c474f81-31d9-5f59-b444-b5bb64d5eb0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163022/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :answer/id #uuid "f931466c-2aae-56ac-8d4e-2932f606b89f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163022/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8eaa02c2-f3ef-5756-a6a3-3874cf4e1b7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163022/selection/b937b5a9c9148a5914243385a1d84bacb019d6c5ff771ce01182a0f3091b9285" :answer-field/choices ["q-163022/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38" "q-163022/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-163022/selection/b937b5a9c9148a5914243385a1d84bacb019d6c5ff771ce01182a0f3091b9285" "q-163022/selection/fea7f6b22e69e29a9716f674d580a63eca4b26e1b4ae5c4f38b3026c28b2b97d" "q-163022/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163022" :question/id #uuid "5747675c-28bb-5974-9009-1516474ab751" :question/math-academy-id "q-163022" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/54e5dd5fdea01c02b968a6040068e190676841cb8d7b7fc05c561e02d522bbf1.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}.$ Given that the mass of the rod is $\\frac{15}{32}$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}},\\,a=1,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nSo,  the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{3}{4})}{(\\frac{15}{32})}=\\frac{8}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163022/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163022"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12475"] :question/problem "The thin rod below has the mass density function $\\lambda(x) =2x\\, \\textrm{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/8c8386ff979b46cd994f1ace60f681a6590856e6960e7d74c71a29bb3f0f2d1a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a \\leq x \\leq b,$ if $\\lambda(x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm = \\int_a^b \\lambda(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x) = 2x, \\qquad \na=1, \\qquad \nb=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{2}]_{1}^{3} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $8\\,\\textrm{kg}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12473"] :question/problem "The thin rod below has the mass density function $\\lambda (x) = (x+4)\\,\\textrm{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/7f88ca365b75320795e9d38170a8586399d759696638a4bd78c73ca6c6f44b1a.png)" :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda(x)$ for $a \\leq x \\leq b$ is given by \n\n$$\nM_O = \\int_a^b x\\, \\lambda(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x) = x+4, \\qquad \na=0, \\qquad \nb=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot (x+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}+4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}+2\\cdot {3}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $27\\,\\textrm{kg}\\cdot \\textrm{m}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12474"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/461c4cb760541ea435620803689e193d13c9cb4706a59b031d37da6ffd49ab9f.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x) = x^3.$ Given that the rod's mass is $4$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a \\leq x \\leq b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda(x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\int_a^b \\lambda (x) \\: \\textrm{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_O = \\int_a^b \\, x\\lambda (x) \\: \\textrm{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x) = x^3, \\qquad \na=0, \\qquad \nb=2.\n$$\n\nSo,  the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(32-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overline{x}= \\dfrac{M_O}{m} = \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{32}{5}\\right)}{4} = \\dfrac{8}{5}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that this result makes intuitive sense. Since $\\lambda$ is an increasing function of $x,$ we would expect the center of mass to be located closer to the right endpoint and further from the left endpoint." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
